  "lineage": "Gospel music of Black British churches, rooted in the Pentecostal and other Black-majority congregations founded by Caribbean migrants after the Second World War and later by West African communities, with choirs singing in a style drawn from African American gospel. The London Community Gospel Choir, founded in 1982, took it to concert and television audiences, and the Kingdom Choir's performance of 'Stand by Me' at a 2018 royal wedding led to a Sony album.",
